<h2 id="faq-heading">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
<div class="usa-accordion usa-accordion--bordered usa-accordion--multiselectable" data-allow-multiple="">
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="faq-1">What is a trough conveyor?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-1" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>A trough conveyor shapes a flat belt into a concave U-shape using angled idler rollers. This troughed profile roughly doubles to triples carrying capacity over a flat belt and prevents bulk material from spilling off the edges. It is the standard conveyor for mining, aggregate, grain, and cement handling.</p>

</div>
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-2">What is a troughing idler?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-2" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>A troughing idler is a set of rollers arranged in a V or U shape. Standard three-roll idlers have one flat center roller and two angled wing rollers at 20°, 35°, or 45°. Five-roll idlers add extra wing rollers for deeper troughs on wide belts. Impact, training, and return idlers serve specialized support functions.</p>

</div>
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-3">Trough conveyor vs. flat belt conveyor?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-3" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>Trough conveyors shape the belt into a U-profile for roughly two to three times more bulk material capacity. Flat belts stay horizontal on a slider bed for packaged goods, boxes, and unit loads. Trough conveyors dominate bulk handling (ore, grain, sand). Flat belts dominate <a href="/industries/packaging-line-conveyors/">packaging</a> and distribution.</p>

</div>
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-4">How far can a trough conveyor transport material?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-4" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>From short in-plant runs to overland systems many miles long. Voith reports a 16.3-mile single flight without a mid-belt drive on the Dune Express system. Long-distance overland conveyors use steel-cord reinforced belts and can replace haul trucks in mining. Practical length depends on belt tension rating, drive power, material weight, terrain, and whether horizontal curves are required.</p>

</div>
</div>
